    "updated_at": "2025-04-23T23:56:39Z",
    "body": "Note that the current `HTMLCanvasElement#captureStream()` is not specced here but at https://w3c.github.io/mediacapture-fromelement/#dom-htmlcanvaselement-capturestream\n\nThen, for `OffscreenCanvas`, per specs[^1], you can actually call `captureStream()` from the placeholder `<canvas>` (on which you called `transferToOffscreen()`), or for 100% non-DOM setups, you can feed a [VideoTrackGenerator](https://w3c.github.io/mediacapture-transform/#videotrackgenerator) with `VideoFrame` objects generated from your `OffscreenCanvas`.\n\n[^1]: Firefox throws when trying to do so, and Safari seems to have a bug where they lose the display of the placeholder `<canvas>` for the first frame, if still.",
